The future of AI shouldn’t belong only to big platforms.

It should also belong to individuals.

Private.
Personal.
Aligned with the person who uses it.

AI that remembers what matters.
Protects your data.
Adapts to your life.
Works for you—not just the company hosting it.

That’s the direction I believe matters most right now.

We’re still early.
But the next wave of AI will be far more human than people expect.

